# Crystal Imperium play test: every move's animation ends at FAST BATTLES' double speed
# (DECISIONS.md D38). The second step a frame must not break an animation that waits for something
# done once a frame (0.13.0's first build hung on Tailwind: a hardware palette fade stepped twice a
# frame never finished). MEW (Lv 50) against Youngster Joey's RATTATA: from the first action menu,
# each move from 1 to the last (no Z-Moves or Max Moves) is put in MEW's first slot and used once;
# RATTATA's battle HP is set to 999 so damage doesn't end the battle (not for Population Bomb's ten
# hits, which never get back to the menu against that HP, on 0.12.0 as well). Belch and Stuff
# Cheeks can't be chosen without a Berry and are left out. Each move passes when the action menu is
# back, or the battle is over (MEW fainted, e.g. Explosion; a one-hit KO).
!new_game()
!give_mon(151, 50)
!no_care_packages()
!battle_trainer(7)
waituntil32 {gBattlerControllerFuncs} {HandleInputChooseAction@battle_controller_player} 1500 A action_menu
savestate menu.ss
!move_animation_sweep("menu.ss")
